From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 16 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: dts: turris1x: ignore the SD card write-protect

The Turris 1.x has a microSD slot, so there is no write-protect
contact at all, and the eSDHC WP input is left floating. Without
"disable-wp" the fsl-esdhc driver reads the write-protect state from
the WPSPL bit, which then depends on the floating pin: the very same
card comes up read-write on one boot and read-only on another, and on
the read-only boots the overlay cannot be mounted and the system loses
its configuration.

Tell the mmc core to ignore the write-protect state.

Other boards with the same kind of slot solve this the same way: the
CZ.NIC Turris MOX describes its WP input with "wp-inverted" in
armada-3720-turris-mox.dts, and the imx8mp-phyboard-pollux added
"disable-wp" for an unconnected WP line in commit "arm64: dts:
imx8mp-phyboard-pollux: Disable write-protect on SD card".

Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
---
 arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts
+++ b/arch/powerpc/boot/dts/turris1x.dts
@@ -248,6 +248,7 @@
 		sdhc@2e000 {
 			bus-width = <4>;
 			cd-gpios = <&gpio 8 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			disable-wp;
 		};
 	};
 
